  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_purse_cb1280faa43caa96928984934093c61f19df4c81f62d54058b80f8193b207446a47">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>purse (OED s.v. purse n.) (see also purs(s)e) | purse (see also porss) | wire used in making purses (OED s.v. purse n. 11) | bags for manufacturing purses | purse, a small pouch or bag of leather or other flexible material, used for carrying money on the person; originally a small bag drawn together at the mouth with a thong or strings (OED s.v. purse n. 1a), here made in Venice | a ring for closing a pouch or purse (OED s.v. pouch-ring) | purse, a small pouch or bag of leather or other flexible material, used for carrying money on the person; originally a small bag drawn together at the mouth with a thong or strings (OED s.v. purse n. 1a) | purse | purse, a small pouch or bag of leather or other flexible material, used for carrying money on the person; originally a small bag drawn together at the mouth with a thong or strings (OED s.v. purse n. 1a), here made of leather | lining for a purse | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch (OED s.v. burse) | as a packing unit for wax | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch (OED s.v. burse), made of the skin of a roe: a small species of deer (capreolus capraea) inhabiting various parts of Europe and Asia (OED s.v. roe1) | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch (OED s.v. burse), here made of cloth of gold | purse, money-bag; bag, pouch, made of straw</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
